           <h3>Spacetime</h3>
           <p>Choose MODIS Terra, MODIS Aqua, VIIRS Suomi NPP, or VIIRS NOAA-20, then choose a date in the timeline and select <strong>View</strong>. Coverage depends on the satellite and imagery available for that day; black or empty areas can be genuine gaps. The lighting controls follow the selected date.</p>
 
+          <h3>Gaia</h3>
+          <p>Gaia lists every image layer NASA GIBS offers, such as clouds, vegetation, fires, aerosols, ocean colour, snow and ice. Use the category chips or the search box to narrow the list, then select a layer to draw its live tiles over the globe. If a layer changes over time, the timeline appears: use the arrows, the day strip, or the date box to step through its observations. Layers differ in resolution and coverage, so empty areas can be genuine gaps.</p>
+
           <h3>Stargaze</h3>
           <p>Drag to look around the sky and select a star to identify it. Set the UTC date and time in <strong>Sky conditions</strong>, or choose <strong>Today</strong> to return to the current time. The light-pollution control changes the faintest visible stars.</p>
